{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786914659964},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a data analysis question that requires:\n1. The total number of farmers markets in the U.S.\n2. The U.S. census data (population)\n3. Calculating farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n\nLet me follow the procedure from the AGENTS.md:\n\n1. **Orient** - Check for semantic models and existing aliases first\n2. **Ingest** the data sources if not already in catalog\n3. **Compute** the values using xorq_select\n4. **Verify** using xorq_verify\n5. **Check lineage** with xorq_check_lineage\n\nLet me start by checking the semantic models and existing aliases in the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents using the xorq catalog. Let me start by orienting to the catalog and then ingesting the data sources."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_017faZRQmo7LorUW1HGNT4Qi","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_017wS1Pwt2A4auwYWGGu9vVV","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":320,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8153,"totalTokens":8483,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0016,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01019125,"total":0.011801250000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":164},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914659987,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77bYGGDjBcNDcCp4DvG","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_017faZRQmo7LorUW1HGNT4Qi","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No semantic models in this catalog — fall back to the ordinary ingest/compose flow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914665754},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_017wS1Pwt2A4auwYWGGu9vVV","toolName":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No aliases.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914665754},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest both data sources:\n1. Farmers markets: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\n2. Census data: https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\n\nI'll need to:\n1. Create build scripts for each data source\n2. Build and add them to the catalog\n3. Then create a composed alias that calculates the metric\n4. Finally verify the result\n\nLet me start by creating the build scripts.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"No existing aliases. I'll ingest both data sources and create a metric to calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me create build scripts for each source."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Y4TMnGKq6V5UD48B9mz2Tf","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p .xorq/scripts"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":263,"cacheRead":8153,"cacheWrite":417,"totalTokens":8847,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0013150000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0008153,"cacheWrite":0.00052125,"total":0.00266555},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":163},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914665755,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77bvhPP5RybqAWkYak7","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","to